  "rationale": "Comparison for unit:shared.typing.expressions against lean:Shared/Typing:ExprTyped, lean:Shared/Typing:ArgsTyped, lean:Shared/TypingViews:StructType, lean:Shared/TypingViews:initialPermission. ExprTyped.giveShare now adds StructType to the successful static give premises and keeps the resulting view. ExprTyped.new uses initialPermission(kind), left-to-right ArgsTyped for whole declared field types and a struct-field guard consistent with well-formed declarations. Weakening preserves permission. The remaining admissibility premises implement the stated normalized-type convention, not an operational-success premise. Notation and judgment context was checked in unit:shared.declarations, unit:shared.struct, unit:shared.typing.giving, unit:shared.typing.weakening, unit:shared.typing.declarations, unit:shared.syntax, unit:shared.typing.normalization.",
